Kind: widen
Issue: #750
Holds open: a processor parked in ring 3, in every boot of entry 55 -- a processor parked on a task's thread is reported with that thread's own frame from ring 3 (pcb->user), its rip, cs and rbp as the task left them, as though the NMI had landed in the task a moment later; -t holds one such processor inside the tick that landed in its task's code, so the report always meets one. Without it the condition came in 1 boot of 32 on omen at 7ce400ae, and 750-ring3-frame-walked was never met; the fixed tree must still pass, each such processor said in ring 3 and not walked

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/ddb.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/ddb.c
index b37db3bb..6956e6da 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/ddb.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/ddb/ddb.c
@@ -875,6 +875,7 @@ static volatile long		ddb_owner = DDB_NOBODY;
 static volatile int		ddb_parked[NCPUS];
 static volatile int		ddb_stop_sent[NCPUS];
 static struct trap_frame	*ddb_frame[NCPUS];
+static struct trap_frame	widen_user_frame[NCPUS];
 
 /*
  * Called from the NMI arm of trap_dispatch().  Answers TRUE when this NMI was
@@ -890,9 +891,24 @@ static struct trap_frame	*ddb_frame[NCPUS];
  */
 static void park_until_released(struct trap_frame *frame)
 {
-	unsigned me = cpu_number();
+	unsigned	me = cpu_number();
+	thread_act_t	act = current_act();
 
 	ddb_frame[me] = frame;
+	/*
+	 * WIDEN (#750): a processor parked on a task's thread is reported with
+	 * that thread's own frame from ring 3, where it resumes, as though the
+	 * NMI had landed in the task a moment later.  -t holds one such
+	 * processor inside the tick that landed in its task's code, so every
+	 * boot of entry 55 has one parked in ring 3.
+	 */
+	if ((frame->cs & 3) == 0 && act != THR_ACT_NULL
+	    && act->task != kernel_task && act->mact.xxx_pcb.user != 0
+	    && readable((uint64_t)(uintptr_t) act->mact.xxx_pcb.user,
+			sizeof(struct trap_frame))) {
+		widen_user_frame[me] = *act->mact.xxx_pcb.user;
+		ddb_frame[me] = &widen_user_frame[me];
+	}
 	ddb_parked[me] = 1;
 
 	while (ddb_owner >= 0 && ddb_owner != (int) me)
